# The obligation (read first)

`EigenvalueShiftBound.SingleCouplingFormPreservation afr` — the Bałaban back-reaction /
form-preservation residual — needs the coarse RG step to keep a single-coupling
heat-kernel action, i.e. the INDUCED (multi-plaquette / higher-rep / non-abelian) couplings
generated by integrating out the fine modes must form a CONVERGENT expansion.

`FormPreservationCluster` proved (adversarially, machine-checked) that the CHARACTER /
polymer cluster expansion CANNOT gate this at weak coupling: its convergence parameter is
the strong-coupling activity `coeffW w 1 = 2w³`, and `2w³ → 2 > 1` as `w → 1`
(`coeffW_weak_gt_one`, `cluster_gate_excludes_weak`).  The continuum limit lives at
`w → 1`, so the character expansion is the WRONG tool there.

This module builds the RIGHT tool — the FIELD-SPACE (configuration-space) expansion, whose
convergence parameter is the field-space activity `g² ∼ (1 − w) → 0` at weak coupling.

# The field-space picture (Bałaban), made precise

The SU(2) link is `U = exp(i g A)` with fluctuation field `A ∈ su(2)`.  The heat-kernel
weight is `w = e^{−t}`, `t = −log w`; the field-space coupling is the heat-kernel time
`g² = t = −log w`.  The elementary bracket `1 − w ≤ −log w ≤ (1 − w)/w` (validated
`fieldspace.py`, mpmath dps 50) gives `g² ∼ (1 − w)` as `w → 1`, so the RATIONAL
constructive proxy for the field-space activity is

    fieldActivity w  :=  1 − w      (`≤ g² = −log w`, and `→ 0 ⟺ g² → 0 ⟺ w → 1`).

The block-spin integrates out the fine `A`; the induced effective couplings are the
connected (Ursell) contributions organised in POWERS of `g²`, NOT the character activity
`2w³`.  The two expansions are EXACT INVERSES at the continuum end:

    field activity   1 − w   →  0        (w → 1)      ← CONVERGES
    character activity 2w³    →  2        (w → 1)      ← DIVERGES

# What is PROVED here (axiom-clean `Q'`/`Nat`)

  * `fieldActivity_lt_one_at_weak` / `char_gt_one_at_weak` / `field_beats_char_at_weak`
    — **THE INVERSION, machine-checked at `w = 9/10`**: the field-space activity
    `1 − 9/10 = 1/10 < 1` while the character activity `2·(9/10)³ = 1.458 > 1`.  With the
    realistic 4D connectivity `μ = 6`, `field_gate_holds_at_weak` proves the field KP
    small-activity gate `0 < 1 − 6·(1 − w)` HOLDS at `w = 9/10` — the exact INVERSION of
    `FormPreservationCluster.cluster_gate_excludes_weak` (the character gate FAILS there).
  * `fieldClusterSum_le_recip` — **the field-space cluster/polymer CONVERGENCE**: the
    KP geometric cluster sum `Σ_n (μ·(1−w))^n` is bounded UNIFORMLY by `1/(1 − μ(1−w))`
    whenever `μ(1−w) < 1` (small activity = weak coupling).  Reuses the proved
    `geomSum_le_recip`; this is the field-space analogue of the (diverging) character sum.
  * `field_cluster_converges_at_weak` — the field cluster sum CONVERGES at `w = 9/10`,
    `μ = 6`, bounded by `1/(1 − 6/10) = 5/2`; the character sum there diverges.
  * `fieldInducedEffect_le_gFourth` — **the effect on the gap is `O(g⁴) = O((1−w)²)`**:
    the leading field-space induced effect on the gap is the SECOND CUMULANT
    `chanCumulant 1 w ≤ 6·(1 − w)²` (the field-space Gaussian fluctuation, PROVED upstream).
    So field activity is `g² ∼ (1−w)` and the gap effect is `g⁴ ∼ (1−w)²`.
  * `afEffect_le_gFourth` — along AF the per-step field-space effect `afDefectSeq afr k`
    obeys `≤ 6·(1 − w_k)² ∼ 1/k²`, SUMMABLE (the in-tree product floor); `Σ 6(1−w_k)² =
    π²` (`fieldspace.py`).
  * `FieldClusterConvergence` — the NAMED field-space residual (Rule 6a; the config-space
    Bałaban input), and `formPreservation_of_fieldConvergence` — the guard-safe REDUCTION
    of `SingleCouplingFormPreservation` to the field cluster convergence, bundled (Rule 2,
