# HONEST SUBSTRATE VERDICT (adversarial — AGENTS.md Rule 6/9)

The library is ENTIRELY the character basis.  It does NOT carry the configuration-space
objects: the fluctuation field `A ∈ su(2)`, the field-space Gaussian measure `Dξ`, or the
connected Ursell amplitudes over field configurations.  What it CAN carry — and what this
module builds — is the SCALAR field-space scaffold: the activity `g² ∼ (1−w)`, its cluster
sum as a geometric series and its CONVERGENCE for small activity (correctly oriented,
`fieldClusterSum_le_recip`), the machine-checked INVERSION at weak coupling
(`field_beats_char_at_weak`), and the `O(g⁴) = O((1−w)²)` effect on the gap
(`fieldInducedEffect_le_gFourth`, the proved second cumulant).

The genuine remaining tool = the amplitude bound `|z_n(w)| ≤ (μ·g²)^n` for the REAL
connected field-space cluster amplitudes, which needs the config-space Gaussian measure —
i.e. the actual 4D YM measure construction, a NEW SUBSTRATE this library lacks.  It is
carried honestly as the OPEN field `FieldClusterConvergence.inducedBound` (the config-space
Bałaban estimate).  `SingleCouplingFormPreservation` is REDUCED (guard-safe, conditional)
to `FieldClusterConvergence` — the correctly-oriented cluster convergence — which, UNLIKE
the character `ClusterActivityBound`, is SATISFIABLE at weak coupling
(`field_gate_holds_at_weak`).  No guarded frontier bundle is inhabited; nothing is faked;
the 4D Yang–Mills mass gap remains OPEN.

# Axiom-gate (AGENTS.md Rule 1 / Rule 8)

